> "We need to count the number of distinct substrings of `s` that are good"  
> A substring `t` (of `s`) is good ⇨ for **each** rule `(p, l, r)`: `l ≤ count_occurrences(t, p) ≤ r`

This count function: `count_occurrences(t, p)` is **determined** only by `t` and `p`. But in most cases, `t` occurs **very rarely** or **doesn't occur** at all — so most rules may be violated unless `t` matches a pattern that appears in `p`.

